  "question": {
    "text": "<p>L-isomer of tetrose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> gives positive Schiff&rsquo;s test and has two chiral carbons. On acetylation &lsquo;X&rsquo; yields triacetate. &lsquo;X&rsquo; also undergoes following reactions.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c497be06-77ec-4141-a034-b89458b9787d-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 75px;\" /></p>",
