  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The tetrose is giving Schiff&#39;s test means it has aldehyde group. The compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>&nbsp;on reduction with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;give Chiral compound so compound can be identified as&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/125d25da-687c-4baf-b696-16c09d21c9d9-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 142px;\" />. The compound can give triacetate on acetylation.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d8a9fe75-2d6f-4fc6-9224-a40d42307994.png\" style=\"width: 384px; height: 170px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d1719263-02e7-40f5-9e20-eef2a476fb78.png\" style=\"width: 385px; height: 169px;\" /></p>",
